# zirv-managed native compatibility files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md) are rendered
# by `render_generated` (src/commands/ctx/context_cli.rs) from the current
# on-disk `.zirv/context/*.md` sources plus a few hardcoded LF separators.
# Because that render embeds whatever line endings `.zirv/context/*.md`
# happen to carry on disk, its output is not uniformly LF or uniformly CRLF
# -- so `eol=lf`/`eol=crlf` (which force a *uniform* line ending on checkout)
# cannot reproduce it byte-for-byte. `-text` disables line-ending
# normalization entirely: git checks these files out with EXACTLY the bytes
# committed, on every platform and regardless of core.autocrlf, which is what
# `zirv ctx compile`'s byte-exact context-layer dedupe (issue #155 Phase 3,
# `native_file_already_carries_canonical` in compile.rs) needs to fire
# durably across `git checkout`/clone/branch-switch instead of being
# permanently suppressed by an EOL mismatch. See issue #225.
CLAUDE.md -text
AGENTS.md -text
